WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.163
MAID and mental health.

00:00:02.113 --> 00:00:05.329
When the system offers death instead of treatment.

00:00:05.329 --> 00:00:12.977
In 2021, Bill C-7 expanded MAID to Track 2 — individuals whose natural death is not reasonably foreseeable.

00:00:12.977 --> 00:00:18.090
This opened MAID to people with chronic conditions, disabilities, and non-terminal illness.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:23.806
The government then proposed extending MAID to individuals whose sole underlying condition is mental illness.

00:00:23.806 --> 00:00:27.784
This expansion has been delayed three times — but not cancelled.

00:00:27.784 --> 00:00:32.568
Veterans Affairs Canada staff offered MAID to veterans seeking mental health support.

00:00:32.568 --> 00:00:36.988
At least four confirmed cases are documented in parliamentary testimony.

00:00:36.988 --> 00:00:46.590
The pattern is clear: a healthcare system that cannot provide timely mental health treatment creates patients whose suffering becomes 'irremediable' — the legal threshold for MAID Track 2.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:50.443
The system's failure to treat becomes the justification for death.

00:00:50.443 --> 00:00:58.454
The Pearce Study at Western University calculated the cost savings: each MAID death saves the system eight thousand one hundred and fifty dollars.

00:00:58.454 --> 00:01:02.556
Fifteen point one million Canadians live with chronic conditions.

00:01:02.556 --> 00:01:06.056
The economic incentive aligns with the system failure.

00:01:06.056 --> 00:01:08.443
The MAID expansion timeline.

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:13.681
From terminal illness only to non-terminal conditions to proposed mental illness eligibility.

00:01:13.681 --> 00:01:18.068
Documented cases where MAID was offered instead of mental health treatment.

00:01:18.068 --> 00:01:20.193
Academic validation.

00:01:20.193 --> 00:01:26.659
The Pearce Study quantified MAID as a cost-avoidance strategy for fifteen point one million chronic condition patients.

00:01:26.659 --> 00:01:29.079
The mental health MAID pipeline.

00:01:29.079 --> 00:01:31.420
The pipeline is documented.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:35.636
The healthcare system fails to provide adequate mental health services.

00:01:35.636 --> 00:01:38.999
Wait times for psychiatric care exceed months.

00:01:38.999 --> 00:01:40.988
Patients deteriorate.

00:01:40.988 --> 00:01:45.022
Their suffering becomes irremediable because the system failed to treat it.

00:01:45.022 --> 00:01:47.954
They become eligible for Track 2 MAID.

00:01:47.954 --> 00:01:50.443
Each death saves the system money.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.272
The Pearce Study quantifies the savings.

00:01:53.272 --> 00:01:57.454
Brookfield's portfolio benefits from reduced long-term care demand.

00:01:57.454 --> 00:02:00.556
The PM holds Brookfield stock options.

00:02:00.556 --> 00:02:06.704
Every link in this chain is documented from official government data, peer-reviewed research, and corporate filings.

00:02:06.704 --> 00:02:10.670
The immigration MAID pipeline feeds immigrants into this system.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:14.511
The veteran suicide crisis feeds veterans into this system.

00:02:14.511 --> 00:02:19.499
The healthcare privatization pipeline degrades the system's capacity to treat anyone.

00:02:19.499 --> 00:02:24.215
And at the end of every pipeline, the same financial beneficiary profits.
